From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: clear the started flag of a stopped shadow
 timer

Only the timer handler clears update_timer->started. If a suspend stops the
timer between a TX and its expiry, the flag stays set and every later TX
returns early from ath11k_dp_shadow_start_timer(). The timer then never
runs again, not even after a firmware restart, because init doesn't touch
the flag either. From then on a head pointer write that doesn't reach the
target stays lost until the next TX.

Clear the flag together with the timer.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
index f389b97ac..18cfb964c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
@@ -1172,6 +1172,7 @@ void ath11k_dp_shadow_stop_timer(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 		return;
 
 	timer_delete_sync(&update_timer->timer);
+	update_timer->started = false;
 }
 
 void ath11k_dp_shadow_init_timer(struct ath11k_base *ab,
